{
  "title": "37: al-Saaffaat الصافات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالصّٰٓفّٰتِ صَفًّا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALSSAAAFFAATE MALAAA-EKATO.\nBy those who range themselves in ranks,\nفَالزّٰجِرٰتِ زَجْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAALZZAAJERAATE ZAJRAN.\nAnd (by) those, who drive away the evil with reproof,\nفَالتّٰلِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAALTTAALEETE ZIKRAA.\nAnd by the reciters of Qur’an,\nاِنَّ اِلٰهَكُمْ لَوَاحِدٌ ؕ‏(4)\nINNAL AELAAHAKUM LAWAAHEDUN.\nVerily your God is (only) One.\nرَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ الْمَشَارِقِ ؕ‏(5)\nRABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA RABBO AL-MASHAAREQE.\nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, and the Lord of the places of the rising of (the sun and the moon).\nاِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِيْنَةِ اۨلْكَوَاكِبِۙ‏(6)\nINNAA ZAYYANNAA SAMAAA-AD DUNYAA BEZEENATE AL-KAWAAKEBE.\nVerily We have adorned the heaven nearest to this world (earth) with an adornment, the stars,\nوَحِفْظًا مِّنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّارِدٍۚ‏(7)\nWAHEFZAN MIN KULLE SHAYTAANIR MMAAREDIN.\nAnd (which is also) a guard against every rebellious Satan;\nلَّا يَسَّمَّعُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَلَاِ الْاَعْلٰى وَيُقْذَفُوْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَانِبٍۖ ‏(8)\nLAA YASSAMMAU’OONA ELAL MALA-E A-A’LAA WAYUQZAFOONA MIN KULLE JAANEBIN.\n(So that) They may hear not (what passeth in) the assembly on high, and they are darted from every side.\nدُحُوْرًا  وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَّاصِبٌ  ۙ‏(9)\nDUHOORAN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN WWAASEBUN.\n(To be) Driven off, and for them being a perpetual chastisement,\nاِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ الْخَطْفَةَ فَاَتْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ‏(10)\nILLAA MAN KHATEFA AL-KHATFATA FAATBAA’AH SHEHAABUN SAAQEBUN.\nExcept, he who stealeth (a word) by stealth then pursueth him a glistening flame.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَهُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمْ مَّنْ خَلَقْنَاؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ لَّازِبٍ‏(11)\nFAASTAFTEHEM A HUM ASHADDO KHALQAN AM MAN KHALAQNAA INNAA KHALAQNAAHUM MIN TEENIN LLAAZEBIN.\nAsk them then (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Are they stronger in creation or (the others) whom We have made?” Verily We created them of a sticky clay.\nبَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُوْنَ‏(12)\nBAL A’AJEBTA WA YASKHAROONA.\nNay! Wonderest thou (at their disbelief) while they mock (at thee)\nوَاِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا لَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ZUKKEROOA LAA YAZKUROONA.\nAnd when they are warned, they mind not,\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْا اٰيَةً يَّسْتَسْخِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA EZAA RA-AW AAYATAL YYASTASKHEROONA.\nAnd when they see a sign they incite mocking (at it)\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۖۚ‏(15)\nWA QAALOO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd say they: “this is but an open sorcery\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(16)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON.\nWhat! when we are dead and are dust and bones, shall we (even then) indeed be raised?\nاَوَاٰبَآؤُنَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ‏(17)\nAWA-AABAAA-ONAL AL-AAWLOONA.\nAnd (also) our fathers of yore?\nقُلْ نَعَمْ وَاَنْتُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَۚ‏(18)\nQUL NAA’AM WA ANTUM DAAKHEROONA.\nSay thou: “Yea! ye shall be disgraced\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ فَاِذَا هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(19)\nFA-INNAMAA HEYA ZAJRATUN WWAAHEDATUN FA-EZAA HUM YANZOROONA.\nThen it will only be a single roar, when lo! they shall gaze (around),\nوَقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَا هٰذَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِ‏(20)\nWA QAALOO YAA WAYLANAA HAAZAA YAWMUD DEENE.\nAnd they shall say: “Oh! Woe unto us! This is the Day of Reckoning;\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(21)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD FASLE LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nThis is the Day of Judgment which ye used to belie\nاُحْشُرُوا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا وَاَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(22)\nAUHSHUROOA LAZEENA ZALAMOO WAAZWAAJAHUM WA MAA KAANOO YA’BODOON.\n(And the angels will be commanded): “Gather ye together those who were unjust and their mates, and what they used to worship,\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَاهْدُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(23)\nMIN DOONIL LAAHE FAAHDOOHUM ELAA SERAATE JAHEEM.\nBesides God, and lead them all unto Hell.\nوَقِفُوْهُمْ اِنَّهُمْ مَّسْئُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(24)\nWAQEFOOHUM INNAHUM MMASOOLOONA.\nAnd stop them, for verily they have to be questioned:\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُوْنَ‏(25)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANAASAROONA.\n( Saying) “How now, that ye help not one another?\nبَلْ هُمُ الْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُوْنَ‏(26)\nBAL HOMUL YAWMA MUSTASLEMOONA.\nNay! on that day they shall be submitting themselves.\nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(27)\nWAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YYATASAAALOONA.\nAnd some of them shall advance unto the others questioning each other.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَاْتُوْنَنَا عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ‏(28)\nQAALOO INNAKUM KUNTUM TAATOONANAA A’NIL YAMEENE.\nThey shall say: “Verily ye did come unto us beguiling from the right side.\nقَالُوْا بَلْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَۚ‏(29)\nQAALOO BAL LAM TAKOONOO MUMENEENA.\nThey shall say: “Nay! ye (yourselves) were not the believers:\nوَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنِۚ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا طٰغِيْنَ‏(30)\nWA MAA KAANA LANAA A’LAYKUM MIN SULTAANE BAL KUNTUM QAWMAN TAAGHEENA.\nAnd there was not for us over you any authority. Nay! ye were a people rebellious!\nفَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآ ۖ اِنَّا لَذَآئِقُوْنَ‏(31)\nFA HAQQA A’LAYNAA QAWLU RABBENAA INNAA LAZAAEQOONA.\nSo now hath been proved true against us the sentence of Our Lord that verily we shall (have to) taste (the doom)\nفَاَغْوَيْنٰكُمْ اِنَّا كُنَّا غٰوِيْنَ‏(32)\nFAAGHWAYNAAKUM INNAA KUNNAA GHAAWEENA.\nAnd we led you astray, for verily we ourselves were astray.\nفَاِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nFA INNAHUM YAWMA-EZIN FIL A’ZAABE MUSHTAREKOONA.\nVerily they on that day shall be the sharers in the punishment.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(34)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAFA’ALU BE-MUJREMEEN.\nVerily, thus do We deal with the guilty ones.\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُۙ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nINNAHUM KAANOO EZAA QEELA LAHUM LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAAHO YASTAKBEROONA.\nVerily they, when it was said unto them that there is no god but God, used to behave proudly,\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اَئِنَّا لَتٰرِكُوْۤا اٰلِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَّجْنُوْنٍ ؕ‏(36)\nWA YAQOOLOONA A-INNAA LATAAREKOOA AAALEHATENAA LESHAAE’ERIN MMAJNOONIN.\nAnd (used) to say “What! Are we to indeed give up our gods for a poet (who is) crazed?\nبَلْ جَآءَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(37)\nBAL JAAA-A BIL-HAQQE WA SADDAQA MURSALEEN.\nNay! he hath come with the truth and did testify the (preceding) apostles.\nاِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا الْعَذَابِ الْاَلِيْمِۚ‏(38)\nINNAKUM LAZAAEQOOA A’ZAABE AL-AALEEME.\nVerily, ye will taste the painful chastisement.\nوَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA MAA TUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd ye shall be recompensed not but what ye were doing,\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from evil inclinations).\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(41)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAHUM REZQUN MMAA’LOOMUN.\nThey, for them is a sustenance known,\nفَوَاكِهُۚ وَهُمْ مُّكْرَمُوْنَۙ‏(42)\nFAWAAKEHU WA HUM MMUKRAMOONA.\nFruits, and they shall be highly honoured,\nفِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(43)\nFEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nIn the gardens bountiful,\nعَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(44)\nA’LAA SORORIM MOTAQAABELEENA.\nUpon couches facing each other\nيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِكَاْسٍ مِّنْ مَّعِيْنٍۢ ۙ‏(45)\nYUTAAFU A’LAYHIM BE-KA’SIN MIN MA-E’ENIL.\nRound will go unto them a cup from a clear spring,\nبَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(46)\nBAYZAAA-A LAZZATIN LLELSSHAAREBEENA.\nLimpid white, delicious unto those who, drink.\nلَا فِيْهَا غَوْلٌ وَّلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنْزَفُوْنَ‏(47)\nLAA FEEHAA GHAWLUN WA LAA HUM A’NHAA YUNZAFOONA.\nNothing therein to oppress the sense, nor shall they be exhausted therewith\nوَعِنْدَهُمْ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِ عِيْنٌۙ‏(48)\nWAE’ENDAHUM QAASERAATUT TARFE E’ENUN.\nAnd with them shall be chaste women with modest gaze, with big (beautiful) eyes,\nكَاَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(49)\nKA-ANNAHUNNAL BAYZUN MMAKNOONUN.\nAs if they were eggs (secured) hidden\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(50)\nFAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YYATASAAALOONA.\nAnd shall advance some of them unto the others questioning each other.\nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ اِنِّىْ كَانَ لِىْ قَرِيْنٌۙ‏(51)\nQAALA QAAELUN MINHUM INNEE KAANA LEE QAREENUN.\nShall say a speaker (among them) who shall speak: “Verily, there was of mine an intimate one,\nيَقُوْلُ اَءِ نَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(52)\nYAQOOLO AAE NNAKA LAMENAS AL-MUSADDEQEENA.\nHe used to say: “What! art thou (too, indeed) of the testifying ones (of the Resurrection)?\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَدِيْنُوْنَ‏(53)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LAMADEENOONA.\nWhat! when we are dead and are dust and bones, shall we (even) then in fact be brought to account?\nقَالَ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّطَّلِعُوْنَ‏(54)\nQAALA HAL ANTUM MMUTTALEU’OONA.\nHe shall say (unto those around him): “Will ye look?\nفَاطَّلَعَ فَرَاٰهُ فِىْ سَوَآءِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(55)\nFAATTALAA’A FA RA-AAHO FEE SAWAAA-IL JAHEEM.\nThen he looked down and saw him in the midst of Hell.\nقَالَ تَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كِدْتَّ لَتُرْدِيْنِۙ‏(56)\nQAALA TAALLLAAHE IN KEDTTA LATURDEENE.\nHe shall say: “By God! thou hast almost caused me to perish!\nوَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA LAWLAA NEA’MATU RABBEE LAKUNTU MENAL MOHZAREEN.\nAnd had it not been the bounty of my Lord, certainly would I (too) have been (with thee) brought into (the Hell)\nاَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِيْنَۙ‏(58)\nAAFAMAA NAHNO BEMAYTEENA.\nIs it then we die not (hereafter)?\nاِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا الْاُوْلٰى وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(59)\nILLAA MAWTATANAA OOLAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\nSave our first death; And we shall not be chastised?\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(60)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAHOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nVerily this is a great achievement.\nلِمِثْلِ هٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعٰمِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nLEMESLE HAAZAA FALYAA’MALE AL-A’AAMELOONA.\nFor the like of this should act every active one!\nاَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا اَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّوْمِ‏(62)\nAAZAA LEKA KHAYRUL NNUZULAN AM SHAJARATU ZAQQOOME.\nIs this the better entertainment or the tree of Zaqqum?\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنٰهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(63)\nINNAA JA-A’LNAAHAA FETNATAN LLELZZAALEMEENA.\nVerily, We have made it a trial for the unjust.\nاِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِىْۤ اَصْلِ الْجَحِيْمِۙ‏(64)\nINNAHAA SHAJARATUN TAKHROJO FEE AASLE JAHEEM.\nVerily, it is a tree that groweth in the bottom of the hell,\nطَلْعُهَا كَاَنَّهٗ رُءُوْسُ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ‏(65)\nTALU’UHAA KA-ANNAHU RO-OOSO ASH-SHAYTEENE.\nIts produce is (ugly) as the heads of the satans.\nفَاِنَّهُمْ لَاٰكِلُوْنَ مِنْهَا فَمٰلِئُوْنَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُوْنَ ؕ‏(66)\nFA INNAHUM LA-AAKELOONA MINHAA FAMAA-LE-OONA MINHAA BOTOON.\nAnd verily they shall eat from it and fill (their) bellies with it.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍۚ‏(67)\nSUMMA INNAL LAHUM A’LAYHAA LASHAWBAN MIN HAMEEMIN.\nThen verily for them shall be to drink over it, a mixture in boiling water.\nثُمَّ اِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَا۟اِلَى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(68)\nSUMMA INNAL MARJEA’AHUM LAAAELAA JAHEEM.\nThen verily their return shall be unto the hell\nاِنَّهُمْ اَلْفَوْا اٰبَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّيْنَۙ‏(69)\nINNAHUM AALFAWA AA-BAAA-AHUM ZAALLEENA.\nVerily they found their fathers going astray,\nفَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُوْنَ‏(70)\nFAHUM A’LAA AAASAAREHEM YUHRAU’OONA.\nSo they in their footsteps did hasten on.\nوَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ اَكْثَرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(71)\nWA LAQAD ZALLA QABLAHUM AAKSARU AWWALEEN.\nAnd indeed went astray most of the ancients before them,\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ مُّنْذِرِيْنَ‏(72)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA FEEHIM MMUNZEREENA.\nAnd indeed We did send among them warners.\nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَۙ‏(73)\nFANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUNZEREEN.\nSee then how had been the end of those (already) warned,\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(74)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from sinning).\nوَلَقَدْ نَادٰٮنَا نُوْحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ الْمُجِيْبُوْنَ  ۖ‏(75)\nWA LAQAD NAADAANAA NOOHUN FALANEA’MA AL-MUJEEBOONA.\nAnd indeed did call on Us Noah, and (We are) the Most Excellent answerers (of prayer)\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ  ۖ‏(76)\nWANAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\nAnd We, delivered him and his followers from the great distress.\nوَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهٗ هُمُ الْبٰقِيْنَ  ۖ‏(77)\nWA JA-A’LNAA ZURREETAH HOMUL AL-BAAQEENA.\nAnd We made his progeny the survivors.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَ  ۖ‏(78)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We did perpetuate for him (his praise) in the later generations.\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ فِى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(79)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA NOOHIN FIL A’ALAMEEN.\nPeace be on Noah in all the worlds!\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(80)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nVerily thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(81)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nVerily he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(82)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We drowned the others.\nوَاِنَّ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ لَاِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(83)\nWA INNA MIN MIN LAABRAAHEEMA.\nAnd verily of his persuasion was Abraham.\nاِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهٗ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍ‏(84)\nIZ JAAA-A WAL BEQALBIN SALEEMIN.\nWhen came he unto his Lord with a submissive heart,\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۚ‏(85)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA TA’BODOONA.\nWhen said he unto his father and his people: “What is it that ye worship?\nاَئِفْكًا اٰلِهَةً دُوْنَ اللّٰهِ تُرِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(86)\nAAEFKAN AALEHATAL DOONA LAAHE TUREEDOONA.\nIs it a falsehood - gods other than (the One True) God, desire ye?\nفَمَا ظَنُّكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(87)\nFAMAA ZANNUKUM BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhat then think ye about the Lord of the worlds?\nفَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِى النُّجُوْمِۙ‏(88)\nFANAZARA NAZRATAN FIL NOJOOM.\nThen glanced he, casting glance at the stars,\nفَقَالَ اِنِّىْ سَقِيْمٌ‏(89)\nFAQAALA INNEE SAQEEMUN.\nThen said he: “Verily, sick I am (of your worshipping these)\nفَتَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(90)\nFA TAWALLAW A’NHO MUDBEREEN.\nSo they turned away turning their backs.\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اٰلِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَۚ‏(91)\nFARAAGHA ELAA AAALEHATEHEM FAQAALA ALAA TAAKULOONA.\nThen he turned unto their gods secretly and said: “What! eat ye not?\nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(92)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANTEQOONA.\nWhat aileth you that ye speak not?\nفَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِالْيَمِيْنِ‏(93)\nFARAAGHA A’LAYHIM ZARBAN BE-YAMEENE.\nThen he attacked them in secret, striking with his right hand\nفَاَقْبَلُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّوْنَ‏(94)\nFAAQBALOOA ELAYHE YAZEFFOONA.\nThen came they (the worshippers) hastening unto him.\nقَالَ اَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مَا تَنْحِتُوْنَۙ‏(95)\nQAALA AATAA’BUDOONA MAA TANHETOONA.\nSaid he: “What! worship ye what ye (yourselves) hew out?\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM WA MAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd God hath created you and (also) what ye make (the idols)\nقَالُوا ابْنُوْا لَهٗ بُنْيَانًا فَاَلْقُوْهُ فِى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(97)\nQAALUD ABNOOA LAHU BUNYAANAN FAALQOOHU FIL JAHEEM.\nSaid they: “Erect for him a building (furnace) and fling him in the flaming fire!\nفَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَسْفَلِيْنَ‏(98)\nFAARAADOOA BEHI KAYDAANW FAJAA’ALNAAHUMU ASFALEEN.\nSo they desired a plot against him, but We brought them low.\nوَقَالَ اِنِّىْ ذَاهِبٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(99)\nWA QAALA INNEE ZAAHEBUN ELAA RABBEE SAYAHDEENE.\nAnd said he: “Verily, I am going unto my Lord, He will guide me;\nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(100)\nRABBE HAB LEE MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nO’ my Lord! Grant me a righteous (son)!\nفَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِغُلٰمٍ حَلِيْمٍ‏(101)\nFABASSHARNAAHU BEGHULAAMIN HALEEMIN.\nSo We gave him the glad tidings of a son extremely forbearing\nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْىَ قَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى فِى الْمَنَامِ اَنِّىْۤ اَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرٰىؕ قَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nFALAMMAA BALAGHA MAA’AHU AS-SAA’AAA QAALA YAABUNAA INNEE AARAA FIL AL-MANAAME AANNEAA AAZBAHUKA FANZUR MAA TARAA QAALA YAA AFA’AL MAA TUMARU SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAL MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nAnd when (the son) reached (the age of) working with him, said he: “O’ my son! verily I saw in a dream that I sacrifice thee: now what is thy view?” Said (the son)! “O’ father! Do thou what thou art bidden; If God willeth, thou wilt find me of the steadfast ones\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهٗ لِلْجَبِيْنِۚ‏(103)\nFALAMMAA AASLAMAA WATALLAH LIL-JABEENE.\nAnd when they both had surrendered (themselves) to the will of God and he (Abraham) threw him (the son) upon his forehead,\nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ اَنْ يّٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُۙ‏(104)\nWANAADAYNAAHU AN YYAABRAAHEEMU.\nAnd We called out unto him: “O’ Abraham!\nقَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّءْيَا  ۚ اِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(105)\nQAD SADDAQTA RO-YAA INNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nIndeed hast thou proved true the dream; Verily thus do We recompense the doers of good!\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلٰٓؤُا الْمُبِيْنُ‏(106)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAHOWAL AL-BALAAAUA MOBEEN.\nVerily, this is an open trial.\nوَفَدَيْنٰهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(107)\nWAFADAYNAAHU BEZEBHIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd We ransomed him with a Great Sacrifice.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۖ‏(108)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We shifted (this blessing) on him (who is from) among the generations (to come) in later times;\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‏(109)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA IBRAAHEEMA.\nPeace be on Abraham.\nكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(110)\nKAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(111)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nVerily he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nوَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِاِسْحٰقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(112)\nWABASSHARNAAHU BE-ISHAAQA NABEEA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We gave him the glad tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous ones.\nوَبٰرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلٰٓى اِسْحٰقَؕ وَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَّظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ مُبِيْنٌ‏(113)\nWABAARAKNAA A’LAYHE WA A’LAA AESHAAQA WA MIN ZURREETEHEMAA MOHSENUN WWAZAALEMUN LLENAFSEH MUBEENUN.\nAnd bestowed We Our blessings on him and on Isaac: and on their progeny are the doers of good, and those (too) who are openly unjust to their own selves.\nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَۚ‏(114)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAA MOOSAA WA AALO.\nAnd indeed conferred We Our favour on Moses and Aaron.\nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِۚ‏(115)\nWANAJJAYNAAHUMAA WAQAWMAHUMAA MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\nAnd We delivered them both and their people from the great distress\nوَنَصَرْنٰهُمْ فَكَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَۚ‏(116)\nWANASARNAAHUM FA KAANOO HOMUL AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nAnd We succoured them, so they were the triumphants.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمَا الْكِتٰبَ الْمُسْتَبِيْنَۚ‏(117)\nWAATAYNAAHUMAA KETAABA AL-MUSTABEENA.\nAnd We gave them both the Book making things clear.\nوَهَدَيْنٰهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۚ‏(118)\nWAHADAYNAAHUMAA SERAATAL AL-MUSTAQEEMA.\nAnd We guided them both on the right way.\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(119)\nWATARAKNAA FEEMAF FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We perpetuated their praise in the later generations,\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(120)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA MOOSAA WA AALO.\nPeace be on Moses and Aaron.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nVerily, thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(122)\nAENNAHUMAA MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nVerily, they were both Our faithful servants,\nوَاِنَّ اِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(123)\nWA INNA AELYAASA LAMENAS AL-MURSALEENA.\nAnd verily, Elias was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI ALAA TATTAQOON.\nWhen said he unto his people; “What! Guard ye not yourselves (against evil)?\nاَتَدْعُوْنَ بَعْلًا وَّتَذَرُوْنَ اَحْسَنَ الْخٰلِقِيْنَۙ‏(125)\nAATADU’OONA BAA’LAN WWATAZAROONA AHSANAL AL-KHAALEQEENA.\nWhat! Call ye upon Ba’l and forsake the Best of the creators?\nاللّٰهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(126)\nLAAHA TAQUL WA LAZEE HARRAMAHAA AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nGod, is your Lord and the Lord of your fathers of yore?\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(127)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA INNAHUM LAMUHZAROONA.\nBut they belied him, so they shall certainly be brought (to account),\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(128)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nSave the servants of God, the freed ones (from sinning)\nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(129)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We perpetuated his praise in the later generations,\nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِلْ يَاسِيْنَ‏(130)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA AEL YAASEENA.\nPeace be on ‘Ilyasin’ (Elias).\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(131)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nVerily, thus do We recompense the doers of good.\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nVerily, he was (one) of Our faithful servants.\nوَاِنَّ لُوْطًا لَّمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(133)\nWA INNA LOOTAA LAMENAZ AL-MURSALEENA.\nAnd verily Lot, was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ نَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(134)\nIZ NAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU AJMA-E’ENA.\nWhen We delivered him and his followers all.\nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(135)\nILLAA A’AJOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nSave an aged woman among those who tarried.\nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(136)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We destroyed the others.\nوَاِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مُّصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nWA INNAKUM LATAMURROONA A’LAYHIM MMUSBEHEENA.\nAnd verily, ye pass by (their ruined dwellings) at morn,\nوَبِالَّيْلِؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(138)\nWABEALLAYLE AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd at night; What! (even) then understand ye not?\nوَاِنَّ يُوْنُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(139)\nWA INNA YOONUSA LAMENAS AL-MURSALEENA.\nAnd verily Jonah was (one) of the apostles.\nاِذْ اَبَقَ اِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِۙ‏(140)\nIZ AABAQA ELAL FULKE MASH-HOON.\nWhen he fled unto a ship fully laden,\nفَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِيْنَۚ‏(141)\nFASAAHAMA FA KAANA MENAL AL-MUDHAZEENA.\nAnd they drew lots, and he was of those who were cast off.\nفَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوْتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌ‏(142)\nFAL TAQAMAHU AL-HOOTU WA HOWA MULEEMUN.\nAnd the fish swallowed him while he was blamed.\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِيْنَۙ‏(143)\nFA-LAWLAA ANNAHU KAANA MENAL AL-MUSABBEHEENA.\nSo if it were not that he was of those who glorify Us,\nلَلَبِثَ فِىْ بَطْنِهٖۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَۚ‏(144)\nLALABESA FEE BATNEH ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\nHe would certainly have been detained in its belly to the Day (of Resurrection) when they shall be raised;\nفَنَبَذْنٰهُ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيْمٌۚ‏(145)\nFANABAZNAAHU BIL-A’ARAAE WA HOWA SAQEEMUN.\nAnd We cast him forth on the naked shore and he was sick.\nوَاَنْۢبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّنْ يَّقْطِيْنٍۚ‏(146)\nWAANBATNAA A’LAYHE SHAJARATAN MIN YYAQTEENIN.\nAnd caused We to grow (to give shade) over him, a plant of gourd.\nوَاَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى مِائَةِ اَلْفٍ اَوْ يَزِيْدُوْنَۚ‏(147)\nWAARSALNAAHU ELAA MEAATE AALFIN AW YAZEEDOONA.\nAnd We sent him unto a hundred thousand (people) or (even) more were they.\nفَاٰمَنُوْا فَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍؕ‏(148)\nFA AAMANOO FAMATTAA’NAAHUM ELAA HEENIN.\nAnd believed they, so We gave them provision till a time.\nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَلِرَبِّكَ الْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ الْبَنُوْنَۙ‏(149)\nFAASTAFTEHEM AALERABBEKA AL-BANAATU WA LAHOMUL AL-BANOONA.\nThen ask them (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Is it that thy Lord hath daughters, and they have sons?\nاَمْ خَلَقْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ اِنَاثًا وَّهُمْ شٰهِدُوْنَ‏(150)\nAM KHALAQNAL AL-MALAAAEKATA AENAASAN WA HUM SHAAHEDOONA.\nOr have We created the angels, females? and did they witness it?\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنْ اِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(151)\nALAA INNAHUM MIN AEFKEHEM LAYAQOOLOONA.\nBeware! Verily it is of their own falsehood that they say:\nوَلَدَ اللّٰهُۙ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(152)\nWALADA LAAHO WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\n(that) God hath begotten: And verily they utter a lie.\nاَصْطَفَى الْبَنَاتِ عَلَى الْبَنِيْنَؕ‏(153)\nAASTAFAA AL-BANAATE A’LAL AL-BANEENA.\nHath he preferred daughters to sons?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(154)\nMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nWhat hath happened to you? How judge ye?\nاَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَۚ‏(155)\nAFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nWhat! will ye not then reflect?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطٰنٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(156)\nAM LAKUM SULTAANUN MOBEEN.\nOr have ye any clear authority?\nفَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبِكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(157)\nFAATOO BEKETAABEKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThen bring ye your book if ye be truthful.\nوَجَعَلُوْا بَيْنَهٗ وَبَيْنَ الْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ الْجِنَّةُ اِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(158)\nWA JA-A’LOO BAYNAH WA BAYNA JINNATE NASABAN WA LAQAD A’ALEMATE AL-JENNATU INNAHUM LAMUHZAROONA.\nAnd assign they between Him and the jinn a kinship, and indeed the jinn to know that they shall surely be brought up (to account on the Day of Judgment)\nسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(159)\nLAAHE LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nHallowed is God far above from what they ascribe (unto Him),\nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(160)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nBut (not so are) the servants, freed (from sinning)\nفَاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(161)\nFA INNAKUM WA MAA TA’BODOONA.\nSo verily ye and what ye worship,\nمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفٰتِنِيْنَۙ‏(162)\nMAA ANTUM A’LAYHE BEFAATENEENA.\nYe can excite not (any one) against Him,\nاِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(163)\nILLAA MAN HOWA SAALE JAHEEM.\nExcept him who goes to Hell.\nوَمَا مِنَّاۤ اِلَّا لَهٗ مَقَامٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(164)\nWA MAA MINNAA ILLAA LAHU MAQAAMUN MMAA’LOOMUN.\nAnd there is not (any one) of us, but for him is an assigned place,\nوَّاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّآفُّوْنَۚ‏(165)\nWWAANNAA LANAHNU AS-SAAFFOONA.\nAnd verily we are they who range ourselves in order.\nوَاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA INNAA LANAHNU AL-MUSABBEHOONA.\nAnd verily we are they who celebrate His praise.\nوَاِنْ كَانُوْا لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(167)\nWA KAANOO LAYAQOOLOONA.\nAnd certainly they used to say,\nلَوْ اَنَّ عِنْدَنَا ذِكْرًا مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(168)\nLAW ANNAL E’ENDANAA ZIKRAA MENAL AWWALEEN.\nHad we a reminder from those of yore,\nلَكُنَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(169)\nLAKUNNAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nCertainly had we been the servants of God, sincerely devoted\nفَكَفَرُوْا بِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(170)\nFA KAFAROO BEHI FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nThen disbelieved they with it, so, soon will they know.\nوَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(171)\nWA LAQAD SABAQAT KALEMATUNAA LEE’EBAADENAA MURSALEEN.\nAnd indeed Our word hath already gone forth about Our servants, the apostles:\nاِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ الْمَنْصُوْرُوْنَ ‏(172)\nINNAHUM LAHOMUL AL-MANSOOROONA.\nVerily they shall be the succoured ones.\nوَاِنَّ جُنْدَنَا لَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(173)\nWA INNA JUNDANAA LAHOMUL GHAALEBOON.\nAnd verily Our hosts, (only) they shall be the victorious.\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(174)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo turn thou away from them for a time,\nوَاَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(175)\nWAABSERHUM FA-SAWFA YUBSEROON.\nAnd (then) behold thou: for they too shall soon behold (their doom).\nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(176)\nAAFABEA’AZAABENAA YASTAA’JELOONA.\nWhat! would they then hasten on Our chastisement?\nفَاِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَآءَ صَبَاحُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(177)\nFA-EZAA NAZALA BESAAHATEHEM FA-SAAA-A SABAAHU MUNZEREEN.\nBut when it shall descend in their court, evil shall then be the morning of the warned ones.\nوَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(178)\nWA TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nAnd turn thou away from them for a time,\nوَّاَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(179)\nWWAABSER FA-SAWFA YUBSEROON.\nAnd (then) behold thou, for they too shall soon see (their doom).\nسُبْحٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ الْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۚ‏(180)\nSUBHAANA RABBEKA RABBIL I’ZZATE AMMAA YASEFOON.\nHallowed is thy Lord, the Lord of Majesty, far above from that which they ascribe (unto Him)\nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۚ‏(181)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAL MURSALEEN.\nAnd peace be upon the apostles.\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(182)\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd all praise is God’s, the Lord of the worlds.",
  "merits": "There are 182 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the total number of Jinn and Shayateen that exist. The reciter of this Surah is protected from Shaitan and is safe from falling into disbelief and Shirk. His angels who record his deeds will testify for him on the Day of Judgement that he was from among those who believed in the Prophets of Allah (s.w.t.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that reciting Surah as-Saaffaat on every Friday keeps one safe from all types of calamities. His sustenance will increase and his life, wealth and children will be protected from the evil designs of Shaitan and the tyrant rulers of the time. If one dies soon after reciting this Surah, he will die the death of a martyr; he will be raised on the Day of Judgement together with the martyrs and will enter Jannah with them."
